  "caption": "Hours per year at or above 35 °C and 40 °C dry-bulb in Dallas–Fort Worth (Open-Meteo, dfw_weather_summary.json). Air-cooled chillers are rated at 35 °C and lose capacity above it. 2023 was the extreme year: maximum 43.3 °C, 99.6 % design value 41.6 °C, 136 hours at or above 40 °C (the DFW station recorded 124). With an assumed derate of 2 %/°C, 2023 had 130 hours below 90 % chiller capacity. February 2021 (Winter Storm Uri) had 50 hours at or below −10 °C, minimum −17.8 °C; cold-weather generator effects are not modelled."
